~ start
Manager: So here is the new tool. Something I put together.
Manager: It's limited on power, but if we get promising results, I can dedicate more compute from the server farm.
=> END

~ part_1
Manager: Yes, that looks like it could be something!
Manager: I've boosted the processing power by 10x! Let's see what we can get with that.
=> END

~ part_2
Manager: Yes, it's starting to take shape!
Manager: What do you think it is?
- Their leader.
	Manager: That could be! I wonder if it's the leader of their team, their nation, or the whole planet?
- Their god.
	Manager: Hmmm... I suppose even scientifically minded people turn to religion in times of peril.
- Their idol.
	Manager: Like someone famous that they want to be remembered? Fascinating...
- A schematic.
	Manager: Yeah! Maybe they found how to bend space-time to make a portal, and they need us to build the other end!
Manager: In any case, I've boosted the processing power by 15x. That should be enough to resolve the final image!
=> END

~ ending
Manager: What the f***?
Manager: Homer f***ing Simpson?!
Manager: Is this a joke?
- What's wrong with that?
	Manager: "What's wrong with th-" - Are you serious?!
- It's your tool.
	Manager: SHUT UP!
- (Say nothing)
	Manager: Oh no. No no no.
Manager: Nobody is going to believe this.
Manager: Every space agency - We've been duped! We're all going to look like fools!
Manager: I have to warn the others...
With that, the manager stormed out of the room.
	The whole project soon came to an immediate halt.
We were all sworn to secrecy under penalty of law.
	The administration waited in silence for the public to forget humanity made first contact.
	The whole story ended up getting buried by the next news cycle of war and famine.
Only a few of us knew the truth.
A civilization was on the edge of extinction...
	And all they wanted to do with their dying breath...
	Was to make their neighbor smile.
...
	And I thought it was beautiful.
=> END